#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

// #taxon[Taxon]
#title[Goup action]

Let $G$ be a group. Any map $X : B G -> Uu$ can be viewed as the group $G$ acting on the type $X(**)$ as follows. For $g : G$, and $x : X(**)$ define

$
  g * x :-= tr_X (l_g, x),
$

where $l_g$ is the loop corresponding to the group element $g$.
